---
import SiteLayout from '../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
---
<SiteLayout title="How this site is built — Vo Thanh Dat" path="/how-this-site-is-built/">
<a class="skip-link" href="#main">Skip to content</a>
<main id="main" class="container review-document">
  <a class="text-link" href="/">← Back to portfolio</a><button class="button button-secondary" type="button" data-theme-toggle aria-label="Switch theme" aria-pressed="true">Toggle theme</button>
  <h1>How this site is built</h1>
  <p>This portfolio is a hands-on learning project in front-end development, UI/UX, motion and accessible interaction.</p>
  <h2>Stack</h2><p>Astro builds static pages with reusable components and TypeScript for experience content. HTML, CSS and JavaScript handle the layout, design tokens and interactions.</p>
  <h2>Design choices</h2><p>Clear reading order, visible text alongside brand marks, consistent spacing and optional detail keep the profile easy to scan. Dark is the default, with an optional light theme. Motion respects reduced-motion preferences.</p>
  <h2>Delivery</h2><p>GitHub Actions installs locked dependencies, builds the site and publishes the static output to GitHub Pages.</p>
</main></SiteLayout>
